  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response and resilience building to improve livelihoods, food security and nutrition in locust affected regions of Namibia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To build resilience at household and national levels, and address post-disaster needs of vulnerable households affected by locust outbreaks that ravaged crop fields and grazing land in 10 of the 14 regions of Namibia. To support interventions meant to strengthen local and national capacities in order to enhance livelihood and dietary diversification while ensuring sustainable and resilient food production systems.</narrative>
  </description>
